Update CICD process:
- I want to get rid of the RC branch
- Instead, the flow will be as follows: active development and fixes into `develop`. Once enough or all work for the next release is done (like Milestone 5 for Release 4 on GitHub), create a new branch called `release-4` from `develop`. PR this into `main`.
- For RC builds, we will still use staging-workflow. but now pointing to release-X branch
- For PROD builds, after merging `release-X` branch into `main`, manually trigger workflow. Allow a text field to enter next semantic version. Like 1.4.5 etc. Add validation to ensure , and other characters does not work. 

Confirm that the semantic versioning works as follows:
- Labels `bug` `patch` etc bumps patch version. `dev-ops` and `documentation` only gets a new build
- Only `feature` and `minor` label bumps minor version

- Manual trigger on `develop-workflow` to deploy to Google Play DEV Internal Track


Dev workflow: distributes to firebase, manual trigger for google play internal track dev
stg workflow: distributes to google play internal track prod
prod workflow: distributes to google play prod

- check if we can remove the `Upload Android App Bundle` steps etc to improve speed in develop_workflow. Same for the other workflows. 